@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ This is the compact durable learning layer for the autonomous quantitative-resea
 - **Observed Effect:** The frontier-first contract is now operative and demonstrated across four new-signal-class cells: activation 37263008074 selected the DEFERRED short-horizon return-reversal cell, executed it with a complete test + independent-verifier pair, and closed it FALSIFIED; this activation (37304873966) selected the next deferred cell (cross-sectional relative strength), executed it end-to-end (manifest, preflight, leakage, regime gate, concentration gate, perturbation sweep), repaired four implementation defects found during execution (off-by-one in synthetic spread loops, missing export, engine-path warmup/compounding mismatch fixed via per-fold constant-share signals, and three sweep/determinism bugs), and closed it FALSIFIED; the following activation (37314710995) selected the next deferred cell (volatility targeting), executed it end-to-end through the same regime + concentration + perturbation-sweep gates with an engine-path cross-check and an independent verifier, wrote check + verifier cleanly with no execution-time defects, and closed it FALSIFIED with uniformly negative figures; activation 37318950814 selected the next deferred cell (momentum: go LONG the previous N-day return), executed it end-to-end (manifest, preflight, leakage, regime gate + 10-asset sweep, synthetic sweep, determinism) and independently verified it (fresh `walk_forward` recomputation MATCH on all per-asset/universe medians and verdicts), closing it SUPPORTED with a REGIME_STABLE positive edge in 7/10 of the universe; and the current activation (37361000967) extended the momentum cell with a real-data lookback sweep (lookback 3 / 5 / 10) across all 10 collected tickers through the walk-forward regime-stability gate with a matched coin-flip null, verified the artifact through three independent gates (fresh `walk_forward` + `noise_benchmark` recomputation MATCH on AMZN/JPM; lookback-5 column cross-consistency vs the prior `momentum_results.json` MATCH on all 10 tickers; robustness verdicts re-derived from the artifact reproduce for all assets), found the lookback=5 edge is lookback-robust for 6/10 assets and 0/10 lookback-sensitive, and admitted momentum to the evidence base as candidate positive evidence.
 - **Decision: RETAIN (verified)** — the frontier-first selection produced a clean ordering (MA crossover -> reversal -> CSRS -> volatility targeting -> momentum), each cell closed with a decisive verdict and no equivalent re-tests; three cells closed FALSIFIED (negative evidence, as expected) but the momentum cell closed SUPPORTED with a genuine positive edge that survived the regime gate, the independent-verification gate, and a post-hoc engine-asymmetry investigation (the apparent reversal/momentum magnitude asymmetry was shown to be an engine warmup+train compounding artifact that understates rather than fakes the momentum edge); the current activation (37361000967) then tested the remaining lookback-robustness question on REAL data and found the edge persists across lookback 3/5/10 for 6/10 assets with 0 lookback-sensitive cases, this activation (current) completed the momentum-boundary review: the cross-sectional-momentum artifact (lookback 63) reproduced exactly via an independent engine walk-forward + coin-flip null path (post-repair verifier: all recomputations MATCH, including baseline null -0.013), verdict FALSIFIED (CONSISTENT_WITH_NOISE; 9/10 sub-universes CONSISTENT_WITH_NOISE, 1/10 REGIME_DEPENDENT (JNJ, dispersion > 2x null), 1/10 REGIME_STABLE (XOM, small positive stable edge); full-universe spread median +0.002 within null tol +0.0305, concentration NO_EDGE, perturbation sweep CONSISTENT_WITH_NOISE). The frontier-first delta remains RETAIN (verified): both momentum boundary cells were tested once, decisively, and independently, with no equivalent re-tests.
 - **Next:** momentum boundary + 20-day breakout continuation cell closed on this universe: short-horizon per-asset momentum (lookback 3-5) admitted as candidate positive evidence; the genuinely new breakout signal class (long on 20-day-high breakout) was tested and closed FALSIFIED (noise-like in 7/10 assets; small, non-lookback-robust positive REGIME_STABLE verdicts only for AAPL, TSLA, NVDA). No new-signal-class frontier cell remains; the next decision-relevant qualification of the qualified momentum evidence is a conservative transaction-cost sensitivity test (fixed cost model, lookback 3/5/10, matched null). A fresh activation should run that cost test through the gate stack with an a-priori cost-robustness prediction.
+- **AGENT_07_AUDIT:** The evidence comparison shows Agent 3 (VERIFIED_SESSION) validated frontier-first selection with IMPROVED task selection observation, but Agent 6 (UNVERIFIED_SESSION) failed controller validation. While Agent 6's content was produced end-to-end (breakout continuation test completed), the missing record fields prevented the system from seeing this as evidence. Therefore, the current focused-task selector is NOT demonstrably superior to prior opportunistic task choice due to insufficient verifiably-validated evidence from the most recent activations using the current selector.
 
